WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Python as labels and boxes.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:12.000
In Python, x equals 5 does not put five inside x. It makes the name x point at a value.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.067
Assigning again just moves the label to a new value.

4
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:26.367
Here a points at a list. Then b equals a makes b point at the very same list, not a copy.

5
00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:33.900
So when b appends three, a sees it too. One list, two labels. This catches everyone at least once.

6
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:44.967
A dictionary maps keys to values. Almost every piece of data in Re-Mind is a dictionary, because dictionaries become JSON almost for free.

7
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:47.500
Update a field by its name.

8
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.567
Let's run a loop by hand. Total starts at zero.

9
00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:57.167
Each pass gives s the next value, and total grows by s.

10
00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:06.600
When the list runs out, the loop ends and total is three. Every RL episode in this course is a loop just like this.

